bds 6,5 "ADS-B aircraft operational status"
date 2026-10-14
preamble
    ADS-B aircraft operational status (typecode 31): capability class,
    operational mode and version-dependent integrity fields. Only the
    reliably positioned fields are decoded; the capability class and
    operational mode sub-fields depend on subtype and ADS-B version.
    Source: ICAO Doc 9871 (ICAO Annex 10 Vol. III) Mode S BDS register definition tables.

items

    TC "Type Code"
        definition
            ADS-B message type code.
        element 5
            unsigned integer
        remark
            31: aircraft operational status.

    SUBTYPE "Subtype"
        definition
            Operational status subtype.
        element 3
            table
                0: Airborne
                1: Surface

    CC "Capability Class Codes"
        definition
            Capability class codes, 16 bits raw.
        element 16
            raw
        remark
            Sub-field breakdown depends on subtype and ADS-B version.

    OM "Operational Mode Codes"
        definition
            Operational mode codes, 16 bits raw.
        element 16
            raw
        remark
            Sub-field breakdown depends on subtype and ADS-B version.

    VERSION "ADS-B Version"
        definition
            ADS-B version number.
        element 3
            unsigned integer

    NIC_A "NIC Supplement A"
        definition
            Navigation integrity category supplement A.
        element 1
            table
                0: Not set
                1: Set

    NACP "NACp"
        definition
            Navigation accuracy category for position.
        element 4
            unsigned integer

    spare 2

    SIL "SIL"
        definition
            Surveillance integrity level.
        element 2
            unsigned integer

    NIC_BARO "NIC Baro"
        definition
            Navigation integrity category supplement, barometric.
        element 1
            table
                0: Not set
                1: Set
        remark
            Defined for airborne subtype with version 1 and above.

    HRD "Heading Reference Direction"
        definition
            Heading reference direction.
        element 1
            table
                0: True north
                1: Magnetic north

    SIL_SUP "SIL Supplement"
        definition
            Surveillance integrity level supplement, ADS-B version 2.
        element 1
            table
                0: Not set
                1: Set

    spare 1
